# Grant user access to antimicrox virtual input devices.
#
# AntiMicroX creates uinput devices (Keyboard/Mouse/Abs Mouse Emulation)
# at /dev/input/eventXX when it starts. systemd user services (like
# ptt-pynput) need read+write access to these devices, but they're
# created with root:input 0660 and the desktop user may not be in the
# `input` group.
#
# This rule does two things:
#   1. TAG+="uaccess" — logind grants an ACL for the active user
#   2. GROUP="input" + MODE="0660" — ensures the input group has access
#
# The install script also adds the desktop user to the `input` group
# as a belt-and-suspenders guarantee.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{name}=="antimicrox*", TAG+="uaccess", GROUP="input", MODE="0660"